Z||000017||Jay||12-04-2001||06:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Its in PISAs catalog. Whats with the quarter windows, I never saw any like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It was trying to copy the Dino GTS.  It's built on an 84 Fiero with a V6 2.8  Someone else did the swap but couldn't get it running.  I bought it for cheap and changed the harness, lowered it and cleaned it up, then sold it.  Last time I saw it the owner made some "modifications" and it caught fire.  I still see it on the road now and again.  It was a Roma kit and it does kinda look like the Dino but side by side with the real thing and it's no comparison!  It'll fool the average person though, because you don't see many real Dino's around.  Here is a photo of the real thing, notice the 1/4 "windows" on the GTS (spyder) they look like this. On the GT (hard top) they are glass without the 3 slots.<BR>"<BR>||||reg||1
